@* App.razor — three @((MarkupString)…) calls of Wasp.AspNetCore.Blazor.Server's
   surface API plus the stock @page-routed Counter. With the gh #80 JIT
   patch shipped, the `@onclick` handler ticks the visible count via
   Blazor's render-diff pipeline; no JS fast-click bypass needed. *@

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Blazor Server on IC — Counter</title>
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body style="font-family: system-ui; max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
    <h1 style="color: #2563eb;">Blazor Server on IC</h1>
    <p>Counter rendered server-side. Click events ride <strong>SignalR Long Polling</strong> over the canister's HTTP gateway — no WebSocket, no external services.</p>

    @* Wasp marker pair around the interactive Counter. *@
    @((MarkupString)Wasp.AspNetCore.Blazor.Server.WaspMarkers.ServerStart(typeof(WaspSample.CircuitOnIc.Components.Pages.Counter)))
    <Counter />
    @((MarkupString)Wasp.AspNetCore.Blazor.Server.WaspMarkers.ServerEnd(typeof(WaspSample.CircuitOnIc.Components.Pages.Counter)))

    <hr />
    <small>SignalR transport pinned to <code>HttpTransportType.LongPolling</code> (value 4). <code>/_blazor/negotiate</code>, POST <code>/_blazor</code> (send), and GET <code>/_blazor</code> (poll) all route to this canister's <code>http_request_update</code>.</small>

    @* Wasp scripts (blazor.web.js + wasp-bridge.js). *@
    @((MarkupString)Wasp.AspNetCore.Blazor.Server.WaspMarkers.Scripts())
</body>

</html>
